From d77facf235a1afd77a97caaed36174a3ebbbae03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Closie <closie@example.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:47:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] feat(android): add robust smart product capture
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Introduce ClosieApplication as the process-wide owner of the single
  LocalWardrobeRepository (no Hilt, no duplicate instances in preview).
- Make MainActivity singleTop and route incoming intents into a single
  one-shot ExternalNavCommand (Import / Edit / Add) consumed by the NavHost,
  so a stale add/edit can never preempt a later share.
- Rebuild quick capture around a single mediaProjection foreground service.
  The service enters the mediaProjection foreground state (ServiceCompat +
  FOREGROUND_SERVICE_TYPE_MEDIA_PROJECTION) before getMediaProjection, tracks
  in-process starting/active session flags (starting only becomes active once
  projection + display + bubble are all ready), gates a late OCR behind
  sessionActive, and tears down idempotently — clearing enabled/running/
  pending prefs and both session flags on every failure path. addBubble
  reports success. One consent per session; bubble taps grab the latest frame
  via OnImageAvailableListener.
- Preview owns its temporary screenshot: back/cancel/finish delete it, "保存并
  继续编辑" transfers ownership to PendingProduct, and onDestroy cleans up a
  screenshot left behind by swiping the task away. Stale capture_*.png files
  are swept at app startup.
- Harden ProductImporter: m.tb.cn/tb.cn detection, anti-bot title rejection,
  robust share-text title cleanup and a share/url/platform fallback.
